From: =?UTF-8?q?Petr=20=C5=A0tetiar?= <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 06:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Plugin: resolve loaded hostapd BSS identities
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Retained AP MLD sockets can outlive their kernel links. Matching a zero
link netdev address or guessing from a one-link interface then
identifies the wrong AP, especially when the desired MLD has already
changed.

Resolve GET_CONFIG BSSID against STATUS radio, band and BSS membership.
Keep unresolved evidence separate from a successfully identified BSS.
Prefer current addresses over a single remembered loaded address. Keep
old identity available during a BSSID change without adopting old MLD
metadata; require the exact active kernel link and the 0008 MLD guard.

An unpark can recreate a socket under the same name without a netdev
event. Keep path availability independent of cached identity. Refresh
connected command and event clients when their server inode changes.

Prepare the private resolver for manager-local reconciliation and the
radio-local removal preflight in the following patches.

Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
